                     /note="'Similar to Synechocystis sp. hypothetical 308.8
                     kDa protein slr0364 TR:Q55582 (EMBL:D63999) (3029 aa)
                     fasta scores: E(): 0, 27.9% id in 2953 aa. Database
                     searches show that the product of this CDS shares >90% aa
                     identity with the previously sequenced Salmonella
                     typhimurium SPI-4 hypothetical proteins: TR:O85315
                     (EMBL:AF060869), TR:O85316 (EMBL:AF060869), TR:O85317
                     (EMBL:AF060869), TR:O85318 (EMBL:AF060869), TR:O85319
                     (EMBL:AF060869), TR:O85320 (EMBL:AF060869), TR:O85321
                     (EMBL:AF060869). The product of this CDS is composed of
                     multiple degenerate repeats. In addition to these the
                     C-terminal region, following residue 1115, is composed of
                     11 large conserved repeats which are encoded by DNA of a
                     higher G+C content than that of the surrounding DNA.
                     Contains a large coiled-coil region between residues
                     105..161. Note that this CDS is significantly similar to
                     the downstream CDS STY4459 fasta scores: E(): 0 33.24%
                     identity in 2118 aa overlap and to CDS STY2875 fasta
                     scores: E(): 27.3% identity in 3025 aa overlap.'"
